#: {{synonyms|en|penetrate|permeate}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Richard 3|passage=Now, while the angry trumpet sounds alarms, / And dying groans '''transpierce''' the wounded air {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Nashe Lenten Stuffe|page=45|passage=[F]oorthvvith her eyes bred her eye-ſore, the firſt vvhite vvhereon their '''tranſpiercing''' arrovves ſtuck, being the breathleſſe corps of ''Leander'': vvith the ſodaine contemplation of this piteous ſpectacle of her loue, ſodden to haddocks meate, her ſorrovve could not chooſe but be indefinite, {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Drayton Minor Poems|poem=To the New Yeere|lines=19–21|page=59|passage=Giue her th' ''Eoan'' brightnesse, / Wing'd with that subtill lightnesse, / That doth '''trans-pierce''' the Ayre; {{...}}}}

